cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Orthonym-Web, please cite the paper below; the software has its own
  DOI.
title: Orthonym-Web
abstract: >-
  Orthonym-Web is the web application for Orthonym, a deterministic, rule-based
  engine that converts a molecular structure (SMILES) into its IUPAC name. Every
  name it shows is parsed back by OPSIN and compared with the input structure by
  InChIKey, and is labelled with the confidence tier that check earned.
